vllm.cpp: VT_DFLASH_DRAFT=1 — the DFlash2 draft proposes through the DIRECT-ARGMAX arm (bundle dflash2.py has_selector=false): full-vocab argmax per block row, candidate selector NOT resident (~254 MB freed). The verify stays lossless (greedy accept = the target's argmax); only acceptance can differ from the selector arm.
vllm.cpp: draft speculative context is limited to 240 tokens (15 pages x 16, 4.6875 MiB per concurrent request across 5 draft layers, so 4.6875 MiB of device memory at max_num_seqs 1 — NOT counted by gpu_memory_utilization). max_model_len is 224 and the (1+k) draft block needs 9 more, so the whole advertised context is speculated.
